From: OpenDesk <opendesk@openharmony.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Mar 2026 13:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix sysconfig.py platform string for HarmonyOS

Problem:
- get_platform() returns "harmonyos-aarch64"
- But distutils returns "ohos-harmonyos-aarch64" (before fix)
- This causes two different build directories

Solution:
- Return "ohos-aarch64" to match distutils and avoid confusion
- Use "ohos" consistently as the platform identifier

--- a/Lib/sysconfig.py
+++ b/Lib/sysconfig.py
@@ -654,6 +654,10 @@ def get_platform():
         # i386, etc.
         # XXX what about Alpha, SPARC, etc?
         return  "%s-%s" % (osname, machine)
+    elif osname[:9] == "harmonyos" or osname[:4] == "ohos":
+        # HarmonyOS/OpenHarmony: similar to Linux, release contains spaces
+        # which breaks build directory paths, so we skip it
+        return "ohos-%s" % (machine,)
     elif osname[:5] == "sunos":
         if release[0] >= "5":           # SunOS 5 == Solaris 2
             osname = "solaris"
-- 
